 r←Test_IE_006(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;ref;code;msg;orig;n1;n2;parms1;parms2
⍝ Test IE with an web page (Google). We need the user to search for something and click a link and judge success.
⍝ It would be really nice if we could automate this fully (SendKeys?!)
 r←T._Failed
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')

 :If batchFlag
     r←¯1
 :Else

     msg←''
     msg,←⊂'This test expects you to search for something via Google. The search page'
     msg,←⊂'should not change except by Ajax requests.'
     msg,←⊂'Please try and when you are sure it works that way then close the window.'
     msg,←⊂''
     msg,←⊂'Any link you click after a search should be displayed in your default browser.'
     CommTools.Pause msg

     parms1←#.APLGUI.APLGUI.StdForm.CreateParms
     parms1.caption←'IE Test Case Number "',(¯3↑↑⎕XSI),'"'
     n1←#.APLGUI.APLGUI.StdForm.Create parms1

     parms2←#.APLGUI.APLGUI.IE.CreateParms
     n2←parms2 #.APLGUI.APLGUI.IE.CreateIE n1.∆Form
     #.APLGUI.APLGUI.IE.Navigate n2.IEobject'https://google.com/'

     ⎕DQ n1.∆Form

     →T.PassesIf 1 CommTools.YesOrNo'Did the Browser control act in the expected way?'

     r←T._OK

 :EndIf

∆TidyUp:
 :Trap 0 ⋄ n1.∆container.Close ⋄ :EndTrap
 :Trap 0 ⋄ FilesAndDirs.DeleteFile n2.∆container.IEobject.∆Filename ⋄ :EndTrap
⍝Done
